# Properties that this device tree defines.
#
# The swap manager's configuration and status (see sepolicy/property.te
# and swap/v521swap.c).  These are prefix matches: persist.v521.swap.
# covers enabled/backend/size, v521.swap. covers status.
#
# They need their own type: without it they would land in the plat
# catch-all "default_prop", which
#
#   neverallow { domain -init } default_prop:property_service set;
# (system/sepolicy/public/domain.te) forbids every domain except init
# from setting.
persist.v521.swap.                            u:object_r:v521_swap_prop:s0
v521.swap.                                    u:object_r:v521_swap_prop:s0

# The two entries that were here in 15.1 are gone:
#
#   ro.sf.lcd_density
#       AOSP's public/property_contexts now carries
#           ro.sf.lcd_density u:object_r:exported3_default_prop:s0 exact int
#       and an "exact" match beats a prefix match in the property
#       context trie (system/core/property_service/libpropertyinfoparser/
#       property_info_parser.cpp, GetPropertyInfoIndexes: the exact
#       matches of the leaf node are checked first), so a prefix entry
#       of our own would never take effect.  Adding an "exact" entry of
#       our own would abort the whole property context trie
#       ("Duplicate exact match detected"), which would leave every
#       property in the system without a type.
#
#       The density itself is not lost: device/lge/v521/system.prop sets
#           ro.sf.lcd_density=320
#       and init loads build.prop before it runs any of the init
#       scripts, in the init domain, which is allowed to set any
#       property type.  The matching setprop in
#       rootdir/etc/init.qcom.early_boot.sh is therefore a no-op.
#
#   ctl.msm_irqbalance
#       The Pie legacy CAF policy already labels it
#           u:object_r:msm_irqbalance_prop:s0
#       (device/qcom/sepolicy-legacy/legacy-common/property_contexts:1),
#       so a second entry of our own would be a duplicate.
